  [added] Terminology
    + (MUST) The Origin provided by the underlying platform is outside the scope of this specification and MUST be treated as an opaque string.
      by: #719
  [added] response
    + (MUST) The Wallet MUST return a VP Token only if it contains a set of Presentations that satisfy the requirements of the DCQL query according to (#dcql_query_lang_processing_rules).
      by: #745
  [added] response
    + (MUST,MUST NOT) If the Wallet does not return any Presentation, for example, because the End-User did not give consent, the requested Credentials are not available, or the DCQL query can be satisfied without returning any Presentation (i.e., all Credential Queries that cannot be fulfilled are optional), the Wallet MUST NOT return a VP Token; if the Wallet returns a response, it MUST be an error response as defined in (#error-response).
      by: #745
  [added] response
    + (MUST NOT) In particular, an empty VP Token (a JSON object without any entries) MUST NOT be used to signify an error.
      by: #745
  [added] http_redirects
    + (SHOULD,SHOULD NOT) If the Wallet receives an HTTP redirect in response to one of these requests, it SHOULD NOT follow the redirect and SHOULD treat the response as an error.
